# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# Both values are safe to ship in the bundle -- see the note in .env.local.
# The project ref is public (it is the hostname). The publishable key grants
# nothing by itself; RLS and the function grants in supabase/migrations/ are
# what actually decide anything.
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=${EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL:-https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co}
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=${EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY:-sb_publishable_REPLACE_ME}

# Not needed to RUN the app, and not read by Metro at all.
#
# Both are COMMENTED, unlike the two above, because the two above are required to run
# the app and these are not. `client.ts` tells people to copy this file to `.env.local`,
# so an uncommented placeholder here becomes a bogus value SET in everyone's environment
# -- and a tool holding a wrong credential fails less clearly than one holding none.
#
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN is what the Supabase MCP and eas-cli authenticate with.
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=sbp_REPLACE_ME

# SUPABASE_DB_URL is lane E's credential -- `pnpm verify:policies`, the only check
# that can see row-level security behave. Leave it UNSET unless you are running that
# lane: it skips loudly when absent and fails when present-but-wrong, and a red gate
# for want of a credential is a gate somebody disables.
#
# The same string is the `SUPABASE_DB_URL` Actions secret, which is what makes lane E
# run on every push. The repository is private, so it has a secret store -- three
# files used to claim otherwise and that is why the lane never ran in CI.
#
# NEITHER OF THESE MAY EVER TAKE AN `EXPO_PUBLIC_` PREFIX. That prefix is precisely
# what Metro inlines into the shipped bundle. Measured: the value of the non-prefixed
# SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN appears 0 times in dist/, EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL's value
# appears in it. A database password wearing that prefix ships to every guest.
# SUPABASE_DB_URL=postgresql://postgres:<pw>@db.YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co:5432/postgres
